  "summary": "Korean traditional craft of decorating lacquerware with mother-of-pearl inlays.",
  "description": "Najeonchilgi features intricate designs created by embedding thin pieces of mother-of-pearl into lacquered wooden surfaces. This craft dates back to the Three Kingdoms period and reached its zenith during the Goryeo Dynasty, becoming renowned for its technical sophistication and the iridescent quality of the shell inlays.",
